title: LSP Folding - (Example)

<!--
A comment over
three lines
-->
\procedure lsp.fr.choose(n)
<%if [<n>match[1]] %>
	one
<%elseif [<n>match[2]] %>
	two
<%else%>
	many
<%endif%>
\end

Open this tiddler's `.tid` file in your editor. Fold arrows should appear at:

* the header fields at the top of the file
* the comment
* `\procedure lsp.fr.choose`, folding down to the line before `\end`
* each of `<%if%>`, `<%elseif%>` and `<%else%>` on its own
* the `<$list` widget below, and its content from the `>` that ends its opening tag
* the code block

<$list filter="[tag[LSP Capabilities]]"
	variable="page"
>
	<div>
		<$link to=<<page>>/>
	</div>
</$list>

